#!/bin/ash
cat <<'EOF'
Lovelace Laboratory commands:
  wuci-lab-status       machine-readable capability and boundary report
  noxframe              launch the bounded NOXFRAME operator console
  wuci-lab-run ...      run a fixed programming-language action in /work
  ghidra-headless ...   run the pinned Ghidra headless entry point
  doas <command>        obtain guest root for system-development work

Examples:
  wuci-lab-run python3 hello.py
  wuci-lab-run c hello.c
  wuci-lab-run c++ hello.cpp
  wuci-lab-run assembly hello.s
  wuci-lab-run rust hello.rs
  wuci-lab-run go hello.go

Guest-local users and doas are not containment boundaries. Do not run malicious
or kernel-level experiments in an ordinary developer/analysis launch. The host
`wuci-lab` supervisor must select a KVM-gated, networkless, volatile hostile
cell for that work; that cell assumes the workload controls guest root.
EOF
